  "title": "Chapter 8: Tripura Culture — Tribes, Festivals, Art and Languages",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "m0y0d8z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.1 Ethnic Communities of Tripura"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tripura is home to 19 officially recognized ethnic tribal communities, with Tripuris (Debbarma) forming the largest group.",
        "Kokborok is the official indigenous language of Tripura, belonging to the Sino-Tibetan language family.",
        "Hojagiri is an acclaimed folk dance performed mainly by the women of the Reang (Bru) tribal community.",
        "Traditional attire like Rignai (lower garment) and Risa (upper garment) highlights the rich handloom heritage of Tripura tribes.",
        "Neermahal, situated in the middle of Rudrasagar Lake, represents the magnificent royal architecture of Tripura."
      ],
      "id": "bs3omdc"
    },
